`ComponentObjectPropsOptions<P>` is an exported type and can validly be used to annotate a hoisted runtime-props object:

```ts
const runtimeProps: ComponentObjectPropsOptions<{ msg: string }> = {
  msg: { type: String, required: true },
}

const Comp = defineComponent(
  props => {
    expectType<string>(props.msg)
    return () => {}
  },
  { props: runtimeProps },
)

expectType<JSX.Element>(<Comp msg="ok" />)
// @user msg is required
expectType<JSX.Element>(<Comp />)
```

This passes on the base, but on this head `RuntimePropsOptions` is already the mapped options type whose values are `Prop<string> | null`. Passing it through `ExtractPropTypes` / `ExtractPublicPropTypes` again cannot unwrap that union, so setup gets `Prop<string> | null | undefined`, the caller rejects `msg="ok"`, and omitting `msg` is accepted. Please preserve the value type and requiredness for already-typed `ComponentObjectPropsOptions<P>` inputs and add this as a declaration regression test.

